<title>GERMANY: East German April adjusted jobless rises 2,000.</title>
<headline>East German April adjusted jobless rises 2,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Apr 97	 Mar 97	   Apr 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.315 mln    1.350 mln	1.198 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.284 mln    1.282 mln	10173 mln</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+2,000	 -24,000	  n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		17.5 pct     18.1 pct	 16.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	65,389	 75,883	   104,442</p>
<p> Vacancies		   48,473	 55,981	   62,472</p>
<p> Change in number in work Feb 97	Jan 96</p>
<p>				-25,000	 -71,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
